y does not contain any repeated joins or scans. Therefore, no transformation is needed for this rule.\n\n**Query Rewrite vii:**\n\nRule 7 applies when the condition involves constants and column values using comparison operators (e.g., `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=`, `<>` / `!=`, `=`). The given SQL query does not contain any conditions involving out-of-range constant folding. Therefore, no transformation is needed for this rule.\n\n**Query Rewrite viii:**\n\nRule 8 applies when the outer query conditions can be moved into subqueries without affecting the result. The given SQL query does not contain any derived tables or subqueries that can be optimized by pushing down conditions. Therefore, no transformation is needed for this rule.\n\nIn summary, none of the rewrite rules apply to the given SQL query, and therefore, no transformations are needed.", 'time': 17.414084434509277}
